 ## Overview
-Phong Shading with SDF Normals is a lighting model for volume rendering that applies the Phong reflection model to surfaces defined by Signed Distance Fields (SDFs). It solves the problem of realistic illumination for ray-marched geometry by computing surface normals via the SDF gradient and accumulating diffuse and specular lighting contributions per fragment. It differs from [Lambertian Lighting in SDF](2023-lambertian-lighting-in-sdf.md) by including specular highlights and from [Blinn-Phong Shading in Volume Rendering](2809-blinn-phong-shading-in-volume-rendering.md) by using the exact reflected light vector rather than the half-vector approximation.
