 ## Background
-Phong shading was introduced by Bui Tuong Phong in 1973. The application to SDFs is a modern adaptation for ray marching. The specific formula and parameter usage described here are documented in a final project writeup for a computer graphics course [S2, unofficial]. The general concept of normal vector interpolation shading is described in the context of R-based isosurface rendering [S1].
